    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on attacking favorable matchups against mediocre arms to maximize our efficiency. The premier play on the board is **Lawrence Butler** (74.61), whose massive platoon edge and positive park factors push him well into the elite tier, even from the lower third of the order. He is followed closely by **Dylan Beavers** (65.38), whose matchup against Arrighetti is bolstered by a high stolen base probability against a slow-delivering pitcher, a vital component of our strategy given the scarcity of speed in this league. **Yainer Diaz** (63.95) and **Gavin Sheets** (63.91) also provide excellent value; **Gavin Sheets** in particular benefits from a soft matchup against Dobnak and a clear SP skill advantage that elevates his floor significantly.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.73). He was the final player cut, falling just short of the 50-point threshold required to displace current starters. While **Jung Hoo Lee** projected well against Woo, he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon and sequence advantages offered by **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Luis Arraez**. On the risk front, we are monitoring the matchup for **Cal Raleigh** (51.36); facing an elite arm like Webb is a clear drag on his production, and while he remains in the lineup, his utility is strictly marginal today. We remain cautious regarding any unexpected late-scratch announcements, but as it stands, the combination of **Bryce Harper**\u2019s reliable output against Manaea and the high-upside speed threats like **Masyn Winn** gives us a projected performance ceiling capable of gaining ground in all five categories.",
